t is built on the ground floor; it means you’re cutting the supply line. --- ### What This Means for Your Question The use of low-altitude techniques doesn’t imply the hail growth zone is low. It implies that the most practical place to intervene in the hail production chain is at the embryo stage, which occurs at lower, warmer levels where supercooled water first becomes abundant. The actual rapid growth into large hail happens higher up, exactly as I’ve described. This is all consistent with the freezing-zone model, which describes both the low-altitude embryo formation (which often happens at temperatures just below freezing, between 0°C and -10°C) and the high-altitude growth zone (colder, more supercooled water, stronger updraft). So rather than undermining the model, cloud-seeding operations actually depend on its accuracy. Scientists wouldn’t target the embryo zone if they didn’t believe the critical hail growth occurred higher up, fed by the embryos and supercooled water they’re trying to control. Your connection is insightful, but it ends up supporting the standard understanding once you look at the details. And hail cannons are just a noisy distraction.
